;; Two things live here, and neither of them is a build.
;;
;; `:paths` is what makes `seal_envelope.clj` and the two app seal namespaces
;; requirable from a checkout, so that the envelope is one file rather than one
;; copy per script — and, since tracker joined cookbook in sealing prose, one
;; file rather than one copy per app. Outside a checkout there is no classpath to
;; put it on, and babashka says so loudly rather than quietly: an installed lone
;; file refuses to start. That is what the `Makefile` beside this is for —
;; `make dist` collects the namespaces into one self-contained script, the same
;; target `us-vs-them` has, and the private deploy script bakes credentials into
;; what it produces rather than into a source file.
;;
;; `test` is the drift control, and there are two fixtures now: one in the
;; cookbook checkout beside this one and one in the tracker checkout, each naming
;; its own app's columns and its own throwaway key. Both are reached by the
;; sibling-checkout idiom cookbook's own deps.edn uses for us-vs-them, and the
;; suites refuse to pass without them. They share `seal_envelope.clj`, so an edit
;; to the cipher that satisfies one app and not the other cannot get through.
;;
;; The third suite needs `sqlite3` on PATH rather than a checkout: the migration
;; walker talks to a database file, so what is worth holding still about it is
;; what it does to rows. It builds its own database and refuses to pass without
;; the binary, for the same reason.
;;
;; The fourth needs neither. It drives the proxy sidecar's own `handle` against a
;; cookbook it starts on a loopback port — the whole path a box's request takes,
;; short of the compose mount.
;; `../tracker/src/cljc` is on the path because tracker's pure seal rules — the
;; prefix, the binding, the inventory, and where prose hides inside an audit
;; payload — are a `.cljc` file its server and its browser already read. This
;; repo is the third reader. Reaching a sibling checkout is the idiom the fixture
;; already uses, and the direction matters: the rules live in the app whose
;; schema they describe, because the umbrella's Docker build copies `tracker/`
;; and does not copy this repo.
{:paths ["." "test" "../tracker/src/cljc"]
 :tasks {test {:doc "Run the seal suites: the shared test vectors, the pure decisions the seal added to plurama_cli, and the migration walker against a database it builds."
               :requires ([clojure.test :as t])
               :task (do (require 'cookbook-seal-test 'tracker-seal-test 'plurama-cli-test
                                  'cookbook-seal-migrate-test 'plurama-cli-proxy-test)
                         (let [{:keys [fail error]} (t/run-tests 'cookbook-seal-test
                                                                 'tracker-seal-test
                                                                 'plurama-cli-test
                                                                 'cookbook-seal-migrate-test
                                                                 'plurama-cli-proxy-test)]
                           (System/exit (if (zero? (+ fail error)) 0 1))))}}}
